- Problem: 783. Minimum Distance Between BST Nodes
- Approach:
The key observation is that an inorder traversal of a BST produces values in sorted order.
So instead of comparing every pair of nodes:
Perform an inorder traversal.
Keep track of the previously visited node using prev.
For every current node, calculate:
 current value - previous value
Keep updating the minimum difference.
Since the values are visited in sorted order, the minimum difference will always be between adjacent values in the inorder traversal.

-Time Complexity: O(N)
-Space Complexity: O(H)

- Key Takeaways
1) Inorder traversal of a BST gives a sorted sequence
2) Minimum difference only needs to be checked between adjacent values
3) Avoided unnecessary pairwise comparisons

